    "faq_XyKTzC": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_row_XdLKBG": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you create a unique website that reflects our brand?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We translate your brand identity and product positioning into a distinctive website experience. Our design scope covers two core screen formats—desktop and mobile—with key page designs reviewed before development.<br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": true
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_ckALeW": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I choose the right platform for my website?",
            "answer": "<p>We help you compare platforms against your business requirements. Shopify suits commerce-focused projects, WordPress supports content-led websites, and custom development accommodates more specialized needs. We assess four areas: customer experience, functionality, integrations and ongoing management.<br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_8DWdMn": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you offer both template-based and fully custom websites?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We offer two approaches: template-based builds and custom website development. Template projects adapt an existing foundation, while custom projects allow more tailored layouts, interactions and functionality.<br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_6Vcq7e": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you redesign or upgrade our existing website?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We can improve your current website’s design, user experience and functionality. Before defining the scope, we review three areas: what to retain, what to improve and what to rebuild.<br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_idcK38": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you connect our website to our existing business systems?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We provide API integration with systems such as ERP and CRM platforms, subject to their available interfaces and access permissions. Each integration defines three essentials: the data exchanged, the direction of transfer and the synchronization rules.<br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_98nUKV": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does a website project take?",
            "answer": "<p>The timeline depends on design complexity, functionality and integrations. Our indicative development phase is 2–10 weeks, followed by 1–2 weeks of integration testing. Planning and UI design are scheduled separately, and the full timeline is confirmed after scoping.<br/><br/><br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_row_yPBYkf": {
          "type": "_faq-row",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will we receive the source code and be able to manage the website ourselves?",
            "answer": "<p>Custom development projects include source code handover within the agreed scope. Handover covers three areas: relevant access, operating guidance and project files. For Shopify and WordPress projects, we clarify the editable components and any third-party licensing dependencies.<br/><br/></p>",
            "open_by_default": false
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
